course: dictionary
lesson: 9472
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and station is one of them. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning the writer means. Ask yourself: what would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
explain: «Britain closed its last coal power station in 2024.» The clues are coal, energy and fuel, so a station here must be a place that makes power. The sentence never mentions trains, so you can leave that meaning out.
explain: «The real reasons are better: astronauts float because they and their station are falling round the Earth together.» The clues are astronauts and the Earth, so station means a building for a special job: a space station.
explain: When the context does not settle it, check a dictionary. Most words have a short list of meanings, and you can pick the one that fits the sentence best.
fact: A station can be a place where trains or buses stop so people can get on and off.
fact: A station can be a building for a special service, such as a fire station or a police station.
fact: A radio or TV station sends out programmes.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, a station is a very large farm for sheep or cattle.
fact: To station someone is to put them in a place to do a job.
exercise: «Britain closed its last coal power station in 2024.» What does station mean here? | A place where trains stop | A radio or TV station | *A place that makes power | A large farm for cattle
exercise: «The real reasons are better: astronauts float because they and their station are falling round the Earth together.» Which meaning fits? | A place where buses stop | A sheep farm in Australia | *A building for a special service, like a space station | To put someone in a place to do a job
exercise: «A Station Road boy shoved Maddie so hard she fell on the kerb.» Why is station not about a train here? | Trains stop on Station Road | *Station is part of a road name, and no train is mentioned | Station means a programme on the radio | Station means a farm in this sentence
test: In «The family drove for hours across the station to check the sheep», what does station mean? | *A very large farm for sheep or cattle | A petrol station | A TV station | A fire station
test: The sergeant stationed two officers at the door. What does stationed mean? | Stopped a bus at the kerb | Gave a warning to the crowd | Sent out a programme on the radio | *Put them in a place to do a job
exam: Which sentence uses station to mean a place where trains or buses stop? | *The bus pulled into the station, and people got off | Astronauts float because their station is falling round the Earth | Maddie lived on Station Road | Britain closed its last coal power station in 2024
